boojum@u.washington.edu (The Vanishing Valor) writes:

>	I suggested the figurine store a while back.

These are already for sale in tool shops. I even got one from a general
store recently.

>1	Potion of Lose Intrinsic (may lose any intrinsic except alaignment,
>	luck, or intrinsics from things that are worn or carried).  Blessed,
>	you may lose two of your choice.  Uncursed, you lose one of your
>	choice.  Cursed, you enter one, and that is the only one you keep.

I don't like this, for the same reason that I don't like potions of
enlightenment: in my opinion, your intrinsics should be hidden, like
your prayer time-out and your luck. Having you actively change them
would bee another bridge too far. Suppose a novice player quaffs the
above potion, and gets asked "What intrinsic do you want to lose?", how
would he even know what an intrinsic is in the first place?

We addicts here on rec.games.hack use far too much nethack slang. You
cannot suppose everyone out there playing nethack to have the same
knowledge of the game. Thus, I would rather see potions of
enlightenment disappear than having options of lose intrinsic.

Losing a random intrinsic could, in my opinion, be a side-effect of a
cursed potion of some sort (poison, for example). A one-in-thrae chance
of the "attrcurse" routine being called, perhaps?

>2	Gargoyles.  When a gremlin turns to stone, it should become one of
>	these ugly, flyin' critters (no steal intrinsic, though).

I like this. The symbol used could even remain the same (g), and they
DO look alike...

>3	Named Archangel levels between the elemental planes.  Raphael first
>	(he's not as nasty as the others, according to Milton in Paradise
>	Lost).  Uriel (regent of the sun in PL) just before the fire plane.
>	Gabriel in the lower of the two gaps remaining, and Michael last,
>	just before the Astral plane.  They would be peaceful to Lawfuls,
>	but since you would have to kill them to go on, a HoOA might come
>	in handy.

This would mean one would have to have a Helmet of Opposite Alignment,
and one would have to don it consciously. In my opinion, donning a
helmet of opposite alignment after you have identified it should
SERIOUSLY damage your standing with your god, and decrease your luck by
a rather big amount (-3 or so). Of course, if you had not identified it
yet, there should be NO penalty, but if you knew it was a HoOA, putting
it on should annoy your god, since you willingly desert him.

